# Rat cradle for the SENSITIVITY runs, moving with the source, in polyethylene (made 5 Nov 2026 from
# the map-derived rat cradle). Geometry UNCHANGED: the same 10 map-derived parts (the in-house 511 keV attenuation map (clinical CT),
# real size, notches included) and the same STL files, placed at (0, {cradleY}, {sourceZ}).
# Only the material changes: Bed_HDPE (polyethylene C2H4, 0.95 g/cm3, coil_bed_real/Coil3Bed.db) instead of the
# map value AC_Plastic_0744 (0.80 g/cm3 as C5H8O2, mu 0.0744 /cm). Why (user, 5 Nov 2026): the map gives the real
# shape and thicknesses (rim: map 6.0-6.2 mm, caliper 5 +- 1 mm); mouse and rat bed are the same white, opaque
# material, probably polyethylene; the map's mu is lower than any solid plastic. Same material as the mouse
# cradle (mouse_cradle3mm_cut80_sens.mac). Volumes renamed ratbed_s00NN (material no longer 0744).
# ASSUMES the map's thicknesses are exact (then the map's mu is too low). If the map's walls are ~20 % too thick
# (rim 6.1 mm vs 5.0 mm), the map's attenuation is right and AC_Plastic_0744 (0.80 g/cm3) would be the better material.
# {cradleY} is set in the main macro (Sens_main_real.mac, setup q86rat), {sourceZ} in its RUN SETTINGS.

/gate/world/daughters/name ratbed_s0087
/gate/world/daughters/insert tessellated
/gate/ratbed_s0087/geometry/setPathToSTLFile coil_bed_real/stl80/bed_s0087_Plastic_0744.stl
/gate/ratbed_s0087/setMaterial Bed_HDPE
/gate/ratbed_s0087/placement/setTranslation 0 {cradleY} {sourceZ} mm
/gate/ratbed_s0087/vis/setColor white
/gate/ratbed_s0087/attachPhantomSD

